From 5a8bdff0172e4a2a346cadcfa4a7bbf001c7b1c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:05:07 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 34/36] Fold bounded native far word loads in speed-optimized
 functions

Admit plain two-byte far loads to the all-users indexed-address walk.
Require the final byte of every sibling to fit Y8; reject atomic,
escaping, call-separated, and unsupported uses. Reuse the original
bounded offset expression and existing M16/Y8 pseudo.

Extend far-index-fold-debug.ll with a -g word fold: the fold drops
the dead pointer's debug location through the same path as the byte
fold.

Default to speed at O2/O3, excluding optsize/minsize/optnone. Retain
hidden off/all controls for experiments. The downstream evidence and
its size tradeoffs are retained in the far-word-index preparation packet;
they are not measurements of this rebased compiler.

Implementation, extraction, and validation: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1
(session source vscode), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort;
verified session 01a0e67f-298f-7a21-80af-06f867085f84.

Word-fold debug-location test added while carrying the far-prerequisite
repairs: Claude Code 2.1.285 (t4-opus-high agent), model Claude Opus 5.5
(claude-opus-5-5), high reasoning effort.
